  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 220 PM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nA warming trend begins on Tuesday lasting through the end of the \nupcoming work week. Southwesterly flow aloft develops over the \nregion ahead of an approaching trough. Another cloudy day is in \nstore across the region on Tuesday due to moist southerly surface \nflow. Highs are forecast to climb into the mid 50s to low 60s for \nmost. The extent of the cloud cover will provide cooler temperatures \nacross the Permian Basin, Lower Trans Pecos, and southeast New \nMexico. The southwesterly flow aloft regime prevails through the \nrest of the work week as the trough gradually moves eastward. \nContinued cloud cover along with low (10-20%) rain chances for \nboth Thursday and Friday are forecast. Warmer temperatures are \nexpected to range from the 60s to mid 70s areawide Wednesday \nthrough Saturday. As the upper-level trough lifts northeast across\nthe northern Plains, this will send a cold front to the region \nsometime late Saturday into Sunday morning, bringing cooler \ntemperatures and low rain chances across the far eastern zones \n(eastern Permian Basin and Lower Trans Pecos). Lows are forecast \nto mainly range from the 40s to 50s with the warmest lows\noccurring Thursday and Friday nights. \n\nLamberson",
